CHAPTER IV
FORMS OF VIOLENCE
Article 7
Forms of violence against women and children include:
a. non-physical violence;
b. physical violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. economic violence;
e. social violence;
f. exploitation;
g. domestic neglect;
h. coercion or deprivation of liberty; and
1. threat of certain actions.

